        "uuid": "4d242b32_0cbbab9a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962375
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T18:03:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "prebuilt etc gen is an interim solution for supporting soong only build until product configuration is fully migrated to Soong. In the long run, we will not be auto generating the prebuilt_* modules from `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES` but check in the modules in the Android.bp files to replace the functionality of `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES`.\n\nConverting all `PRODUCT_COPY_FILES` entries using `prebuilt_any` module type would lead to additional burden when checking in the modules in the Android.bp files, given that `prebuilt_any` module should not be used in Android.bp files. Thus, the auto generation using prebuilt_any should be restrictive and used as a \"fall-back\" behavior, not the default one.",
      "revId": "af3bdffd6393a0ff372bca2c45f03d1f382b07f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f465931d_3606c8c1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081223
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T18:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m all for that, but currently not exposing these modules doesn\u0027t easily let me translate to .bp modules.\n\nWe generate the rules and can easily migrate them, but with the current neverallows in place we _can\u0027t_ do that.\n\nI don\u0027t know how not exposing them can help with the transition, it\u0027s not like we can even extract them directly to be imported in our trees, more so with neverallows.\n\nAlso what\u0027s up with the logic to use prebuilt_any only when base names match? Is there any advantage?",
      "parentUuid": "4d242b32_0cbbab9a",
      "revId": "af3bdffd6393a0ff372bca2c45f03d1f382b07f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e73c8012_1dd44660",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T18:30:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We haven\u0027t decided if we actually want to have a bunch of different prebuilt_* modules or figure out some better design like prebuilt_any or something entirely different. The neverallow rules allow us to reserve the right to remove these modules later if we decide we don\u0027t need them.\n\nWe don\u0027t have any product 100% working in soong-only builds yet. Although the long term plan is to check the generated modules into Android.bp files, we don\u0027t want to do that yet so it\u0027s easy to make changes and just autogenerate different modules.\n\nI personally don\u0027t really mind this cl, if we need prebuilt_any for these random file locations that keep popping up we could replace all the other prebuilt_ module types with it. If it\u0027s neverallowed we can switch back to them later.",
      "parentUuid": "f465931d_3606c8c1",
      "revId": "af3bdffd6393a0ff372bca2c45f03d1f382b07f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19626280_95d3d75f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081223
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T18:41:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I already have 3 more changes to add OEM/ODM/vendor specific modules in our downstream set of open changes, and rather then spamming you all with more of those useless changes I thought it would be easier to simply do that.\n\nAlso I didn\u0027t actually verify but I assume having all those module names reversed to hidden modules won\u0027t let me create them as simple soong extensions with sane names, prebuilt_lineage_gpu sounds rather cumbersome...\n\nprebuilt_any is anonymous enough, and still let you not expose those intrinsics to possible users, until you find a proper solution.\n\nI\u0027m not saying I want this merged, but with possibility of removal of all the current hidden modules (that I have locally in case that would be ok) would allow us to create at least some custom modules with sane-names to migrate to soong only our copy files, and that might be enough for us.\nOur biggest .mk at the moment are those endless list of copy rules of vendor files that aren\u0027t yet Soong modules (everything else is)",
      "parentUuid": "e73c8012_1dd44660",
      "revId": "af3bdffd6393a0ff372bca2c45f03d1f382b07f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcc15d33_91f2bf54",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081223
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T21:03:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 since it works.\n\nI\u0027m sill unsure how I feel about prebuilt_any for everything vs adding more prebuilt_* modules, the latter is just more annoying in case _more_ cases pup up, the former probably safer.\n\nWith that said, it\u0027s up to you ^^",
      "revId": "af3bdffd6393a0ff372bca2c45f03d1f382b07f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
